From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Pulsar Bot <pulsar@localhost>
Date: Sat, 08 Aug 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] futex: implement futex_waitv syscall (nr 449)

Backport of sys_futex_waitv from Linux 5.16 adapted for the 4.19 CAF
single-file futex implementation (kernel/futex.c).

futex_waitv allows waiting on an array of up to 128 futexes in a single
syscall. This is critical for Wine/ntsync performance: games using
hundreds of sync objects can batch their waits instead of making N
individual futex syscalls.

The implementation is self-contained and appended to kernel/futex.c,
reusing existing infrastructure: get_futex_key(), futex_wait_setup(),
futex_wait_queue_me(), unqueue_me(), queue_lock/unlock().

Key differences from 5.16 upstream:
- No separate kernel/futex/ directory; code appended to kernel/futex.c
- Uses 4.19 hrtimer_sleeper_on_stack API
- Uses get_timespec64/timespec64_to_ktime available in this base
- Syscall nr 449 registered in unistd.h and unistd32.h

Signed-off-by: Pulsar Bot <pulsar@localhost>
